---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
---
<Base title={"Inside Our Office | Calming Therapy Space at Tangible | Tangible Therapy"} description={"See inside Tangible Therapy’s calming, thoughtfully designed space. Feel safe, grounded, and at ease from the moment you walk through the door."}>
<section class="sec t-bright h-medium has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:7;--mrows:9">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/4/6/24;--m:1/2/6/10"><div class="rte"><h1 class="ta-center">Our Space</h1><p class="lg ta-center">From the moment you walk in, we want you to feel safe, seen, and at ease.</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:6/11/8/17;--m:7/2/9/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="https://tangible.clientsecure.me/">Visit our office in person</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#fff" /></section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:12;--mrows:22">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/5/12;--m:2/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>A therapy space that feels nothing like a clinic</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/15/12/26;--m:15/2/22/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill"><img src="/images/adobestock-1280114914-99ffb9.jpg" alt="Modern living room with a white chaise lounge, a potted plant, a beige armchair, a wooden sideboard with a lamp, and framed floral wall art." width="8736" height="4896" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/2/12/12;--m:5/2/15/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>Tangible Therapy isn’t cold, clinical, or impersonal. Our office was intentionally designed to feel warm, calming, and human. Every element — from lighting to layout — is meant to help you exhale and settle in.</p><p>We want therapy to feel approachable, not intimidating. Whether you’re visiting us for the first time or coming back for a familiar weekly session, this is a space where you can take a breath, let your guard down, and begin the work of healing.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:22;--mrows:46">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/6/3/22;--m:1/2/4/10;--dz:7;--mz:7"><div class="rte"><h3 class="ta-center">What you’ll find when you arrive</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:3/5/10/13;--m:4/2/11/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--fp:10% 80%"><img src="/images/adobestock-1434553349-298313.jpg" alt="Spa or massage room with a massage table, green plants in pots, candles, and neatly folded towels on a wooden shelf against a textured wall." width="5376" height="3584" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:3/15/10/23;--m:14/2/21/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><figure class="img fill"><img src="/images/adobestock-384782092-914e1e.jpg" alt="Bright, minimalist massage room with a massage table covered in a white towel and rolled towel, nearby white cart with lotions, and a shelving unit with bottles, towels, and decorative items." width="6524" height="4349" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:10/5/12/13;--m:11/2/14/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p class="ta-center">A quiet, thoughtfully curated waiting area with soft lighting, cozy seating, and calming textures</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:10/15/12/23;--m:21/2/24/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="rte"><p class="ta-center">Private therapy rooms that feel like comfortable living spaces — never sterile or harsh</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:13/5/20/13;--m:25/2/32/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><figure class="img fill"><img src="/images/adobestock-607894224-b2ef96.jpg" alt="Empty medical examination room with examination table, medical chairs, and diagnostic equipment." width="5000" height="3333" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:13/15/20/23;--m:36/2/43/10;--dz:6;--mz:6"><figure class="img fill"><img src="/images/adobestock-837418838-008893.jpg" alt="Cozy living room with two beige armchairs, a small round wooden table with tissues, a glass of water, and a square box, a white bookshelf with binders, plants, and natural light from the window." width="5120" height="2880" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:20/5/23/13;--m:32/2/35/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="rte"><p class="ta-center">Sensory-friendly elements like low noise levels, and the option to dim lights or use grounding tools during your session</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:20/15/22/23;--m:43/2/46/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><div class="rte"><p class="ta-center">An atmosphere of quiet care<strong> </strong>— no judgment, no pressure; only room to be exactly where you are</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:22">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/6/12;--m:1/2/4/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2>Accessible, inclusive, and intentionally safe</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/15/13/26;--m:15/2/22/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill"><img src="/images/adobestock-1536860313-ab35e8.jpg" alt="Modern living room with two cream-colored armchairs, a small wooden side table with a book, and two tall potted plants on either side, against a textured, cloud-like wall." width="6144" height="3072" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/2/13/13;--m:4/2/15/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>We’ve created a space that supports many needs, identities, and experiences. Our office is:</p><ul><li><p>Gender-inclusive and welcoming to LGBTQ+ clients</p></li><li><p>Flexible for those with sensory sensitivities or trauma histories</p></li><li><p>Designed to reduce overwhelm — not add to it</p></li></ul><p>Let us know what helps you feel safe or supported. We’re always happy to adjust lighting, seating, or other environmental details to meet your needs.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:11;--mrows:19">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:1/2/12/13;--m:10/2/17/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill"><img src="/images/adobestock-843469970-60b823.jpg" alt="Living room corner with two mid-century modern style armchairs, a side table with plants and decorative items, and large windows with blinds surrounded by houseplants. Decor includes framed botanical artwork." width="5376" height="3584" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/15/6/25;--m:1/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>Therapy starts with where you are — and that includes the space you’re in</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/15/9/25;--m:5/2/12/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>We believe your surroundings matter. Healing happens best in places that feel secure, calm, and grounded. Our space is more than a backdrop — it’s part of the therapeutic experience.</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:9/15/11/21;--m:17/2/19/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-secondary btn-large btn-full" href="/contact">Schedule Your First Visit</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</Base>
